# The STL step bar on the Run page (bug shakedown, 2026-10-26): a setup never edited still writes its case files done;
# the bar keeps its boundaries while the mesh is made; a mesh made after the Run page was opened is not made again by
# the run; controlDict edited elsewhere comes back into the setup; a setup change after a run makes Physics, then Run,
# out of date; an outlet made an opening is the same mesh; a boundary changed on the Mesh tab is what runs.
budget p95 60 max 400
shell mkdir -p $SB/ws/duct/system && python3 -c "import itertools;L=(0.4,0.1,0.1);P=lambda a,b,c:(a*L[0],b*L[1],c*L[2]);F=[(P(0,0,0),P(0,0,1),P(0,1,1),P(0,1,0)),(P(1,0,0),P(1,1,0),P(1,1,1),P(1,0,1)),(P(0,0,0),P(1,0,0),P(1,0,1),P(0,0,1)),(P(0,1,0),P(0,1,1),P(1,1,1),P(1,1,0)),(P(0,0,0),P(0,1,0),P(1,1,0),P(1,0,0)),(P(0,0,1),P(1,0,1),P(1,1,1),P(0,1,1))];o=open('$SB/ws/duct.stl','w');o.write('solid duct\n');[o.write('facet normal 0 0 0\nouter loop\n'+''.join('vertex %g %g %g\n'%v for v in t)+'endloop\nendfacet\n') for q in F for t in ((q[0],q[1],q[2]),(q[0],q[2],q[3]))];o.write('endsolid duct\n')" && printf 'FoamFile { version 2.0; format ascii; class dictionary; object controlDict; }\napplication simpleFoam;\nstartTime 0;\nendTime 10;\ndeltaT 1;\nwriteControl timeStep;\nwriteInterval 10;\n' > $SB/ws/duct/system/controlDict
open $SB/ws/duct
click nav:mesh
wait-until page Mesh
click text:STL mesher
wait 5
click stl-path
enter $SB/ws/duct.stl
wait 10
assert text 6 boundaries
screenshot $OUT/01_loaded.png
click stl-next
wait 3
click stl-next
wait 3
assert text Internal flow needs
click stl-b#4>name
key a ctrl
enter inlet
wait 3
click stl-b#4>type
wait 2
click text:Inlet
wait 3
click stl-b#5>name
key a ctrl
enter outlet
wait 3
click stl-b#5>type
wait 2
click text:Outlet
wait 3
assert file mesher/mesher.ini
note 1: a setup never edited has no simulation.ini: the case files must still come out done, from the Run page
shell rm -f simulation.ini
click nav:run
wait-until page Run
wait 5
click wf-next
wait-until job running timeout 20
note 2: on Run while the mesh is made: the bar keeps its boundaries
wait 2
assert text 1 in, 1 out, 4 walls
screenshot $OUT/20_run_while_meshing.png
wait-until job finished timeout 300
wait 5
assert log log.checkMesh Mesh OK.
assert file mesher/mesh.sig
note the Run page writes the case files itself once the mesh is there (nothing to click)
wait-until file 0/U timeout 10
wait 5
screenshot $OUT/21_run_meshed.png
assert file simulation.ini
assert file 0/U
assert text simpleFoam, k-omega SST
assert text Run simulation
screenshot $OUT/22_run_written.png
note 3: the controlDict edited elsewhere: the setup takes it, and the case files stay done
shell foamDictionary system/controlDict -entry endTime -set 40 > /dev/null && foamDictionary system/controlDict -entry writeInterval -set 20 > /dev/null
wait-until log simulation.ini iterations = 40 timeout 10
assert text simpleFoam, k-omega SST
assert text Run simulation
click wf-next
wait-until job running timeout 30
wait-until job finished timeout 300
wait 5
assert text Results to 40
shell rm -f .qc-no-remesh; [ log.snappyHexMesh -ot log.checkMesh ] && touch .qc-no-remesh
assert file .qc-no-remesh
assert text Open in ParaView
screenshot $OUT/23_run_done.png
note 4: a setup change after the run: Physics then Run out of date
click nav:physics
wait-until page Physics
wait 5
click su-turb
wait 2
click text:k-epsilon
wait 5
assert text Setup changed: write again
click wf-next
wait 5
assert log constant/turbulenceProperties kEpsilon
assert text Older than the setup: run again
screenshot $OUT/24_physics_rewritten.png
note 5: an outlet made an opening is the same mesh
click nav:mesh
wait-until page Mesh
wait 5
click stl-step#2
wait 3
click stl-b#5>type
wait 2
click text:Opening
wait 5
click nav:physics
wait-until page Physics
wait 5
assert text Older than the setup: run again
assert text Write case files
screenshot $OUT/25_type_swap.png
assert log log.simpleFoam End
note 6: a boundary changed on the Mesh tab: the Run page brings the case files up to date, and that is what runs
click nav:mesh
wait-until page Mesh
wait 5
click stl-step#2
wait 3
click stl-b#4>name
wait 5
click inlet>in-speed
key a ctrl
enter 3
wait 5
assert log simulation.ini speed = 3
click nav:run
wait-until page Run
wait-until log 0/U refValue        uniform -3 timeout 10
assert text simpleFoam, k-epsilon
